{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB annual general adjustment 5% cap","requirement":"Measure BB caps Berkeley's Annual General Adjustment at 5%, so that a rent increase for a fully covered unit may not exceed 5% under the AGA for the year; banked unused AGAs may still be used to reach the rent ceiling.","key_value":"5% maximum AGA","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered rental units, including most multifamily units built before 1980, some single-family homes, and government-owned or -subsidized units newly covered; the elected Rent Board sets the AGA annually from a Consumer Price Index formula.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Units where the tenant shares kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord are exempt only if the landlord lived on the same property at the start of the tenancy.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"The cap does not prevent a landlord with banked (unused) AGAs from prior years from raising rent above 5% to reach the rent ceiling.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"The maximum AGA is 5%. This means that, if the formula in the Rent Ordinance results in an AGA that is greater than 5%, the AGA approved by the Board for that year can be no more than 5%.","interaction":"Some subsidized units are only partially covered because Federal law, State law, or administrative regulation prohibits rent control on them.","relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB just cause eviction grounds and notice requirements","requirement":"Tenants in covered units may be evicted only for just cause. Eviction for rental debt under one month's Fair Market Rent or for refusing to sign a substantially similar lease is barred, and lease-breach notices must describe the violation and actual harm.","key_value":"Rental debt threshold: 1 month's Fair Market Rent","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance; landlords must include required notice content and file eviction notices and lawsuits with the Rent Board within three business days.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"Eviction for nonpayment of rent is no longer permitted for rental debt of less than one month's Fair Market Rent for a unit of equivalent size.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","n_rules":2,"note":null}

